==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|free-loader}}

===Etymology===
{{af|en|free|load|-er|id3=agent noun}}, originally US 1930s.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɹiːləʊdə(ɹ)/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɹiloʊdɚ/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-freeloader.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} One who does not [[contribute]] or [[pay]] appropriately; one who gets a [[free ride]], etc. without paying a [[fair share]].
#: {{syn|en|free rider|moocher|Thesaurus:scrounger}}
# {{lb|en|UK|NZ|Canada}} A person who takes [[expired]] [[unsold]] [[merchandise]] from the back of [[supermarket]] [[premise]]s.

